<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">José Ballivián</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1805">1805</a>–<a href="/years/1852">1852</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">José Ballivián was a Bolivian general and president from 1841 to 1847. On 18 November 1841 he defeated a Peruvian invasion at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-ingavi">Battle of Ingavi</a>, where the Peruvian president <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/agustin-gamarra">Agustín Gamarra</a> was killed, securing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bolivia">Bolivia</a>'s independence. His government organised the administration, founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">department</a> of Beni and sponsored exploration of the eastern lowlands, but revolts forced him into exile in 1847.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jose-ballivian.jpg" alt="José Ballivián" width="320" height="481" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Antonio Villavicencio · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jos%C3%A9_Ballivi%C3%A1n._Villavicencio,_Antonio._c._1841,_Museo_de_Charcas,_Sucre.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
